{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-114025" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{9\\sqrt{1-81{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-114025" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $81{x}^{2}=(9x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=9x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=9\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{9}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{9\\sqrt{1-81{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(9x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{9}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{81}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{81}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{81}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(9x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-114025" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c05a08d8162628e21f5cd0f4a253bb7a2733fb49041e999778716cebcb87e247"} {"question" "q-114025" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-114025" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "81\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(9x)+C"] ["math" "9\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(9x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{81}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(9x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(9x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-114025" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{81}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(9x)+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-114027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{8}{\\sqrt{1-3{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-114027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $3{x}^{2}=(\\sqrt{3}x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\sqrt{3}x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{8}{\\sqrt{1-3{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{8}{\\sqrt{1-(\\sqrt{3}x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{3}}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-114027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c05a08d8162628e21f5cd0f4a253bb7a2733fb49041e999778716cebcb87e247"} {"question" "q-114027" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-114027" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{8\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{3}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(3x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{3}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{8}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(3x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{8}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-114027" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{8\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x)+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-114024" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1-2{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-114024" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $2{x}^{2}=(\\sqrt{2}x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\sqrt{2}x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{2}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1-2{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =4\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(\\sqrt{2}x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{2}}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-114024" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c05a08d8162628e21f5cd0f4a253bb7a2733fb49041e999778716cebcb87e247"} {"question" "q-114024" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-114024" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)+C"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x)+C"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)+C"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)+C"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-114024" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-114023" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{6\\sqrt{1-36{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-114023" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $36{x}^{2}=(6x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=6x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{6}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{6\\sqrt{1-36{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{6}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(6x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{6}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{36}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{36}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{36}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(6x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-114023" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c05a08d8162628e21f5cd0f4a253bb7a2733fb49041e999778716cebcb87e247"} {"question" "q-114023" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-114023" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "36\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(6x)+C"] ["math" "6\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(6x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{36}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(6x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(6x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-114023" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{36}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(6x)+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-2505" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-4{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-2505" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $4{x}^{2}=(2x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=2x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-4{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(2x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x)}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-2505" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c05a08d8162628e21f5cd0f4a253bb7a2733fb49041e999778716cebcb87e247"} {"question" "q-2505" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-2505" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(2x)}{2}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(4x)}{4}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x)}{2}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(4x)}{4}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-2505" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x)}{2}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-49550" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{1}{25+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-49550" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{25+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{25\\cdot (1+{x}^{2}/25)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}/25}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/5)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{5})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{5}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{5}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=5\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{25+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{25}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/5)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (5\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{5})+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-49550" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c05a08d8162628e21f5cd0f4a253bb7a2733fb49041e999778716cebcb87e247"} {"question" "q-49550" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type"