resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{8})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{8}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{8}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=8\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{64+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{32}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/8)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{32}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (8\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{8})+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-49551" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c05a08d8162628e21f5cd0f4a253bb7a2733fb49041e999778716cebcb87e247"} {"question" "q-49551" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-49551" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(8x)}{8}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x}{8})}{4}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})}{4}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{8})}{4}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{8})}{8}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-49551" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{8})}{4}+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-114046" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{9}{81+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-114046" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{9}{81+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{9}{81\\cdot (1+{x}^{2}/81)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}/81}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/9)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\n The only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{9})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{9}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{9}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=9\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{9}{81+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/9)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (9\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{9})+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-114046" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c05a08d8162628e21f5cd0f4a253bb7a2733fb49041e999778716cebcb87e247"} {"question" "q-114046" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-114046" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "9\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{9})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{9})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(9x)+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{9})+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-114046" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{9})+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-69477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{3\\,\\text{d}x}{|9x|\\sqrt{(9x)^{2}-1}}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-69477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{3\\,\\text{d}x}{|9x|\\sqrt{(9x)^{2}-1}}=3\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{|9x|\\sqrt{(9x)^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nThis integral now resembles the basic one for $\\text{arcsec},$\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $9x.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=9x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=9\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{9}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}3\\int \\frac{1}{|9x|\\sqrt{(9x)^{2}-1}}\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{9}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(9x)}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-69477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c05a08d8162628e21f5cd0f4a253bb7a2733fb49041e999778716cebcb87e247"} {"question" "q-69477" "field" "