 "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{|x|\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}-1}}=\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{|\\sqrt{2}x|\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{2}x)^{2}-1}}\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral now resembles the basic one for $\\text{arcsec},$\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $\\sqrt{2}x.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\sqrt{2}x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{2}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{|\\sqrt{2}x|\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{2}x)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{2}x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-114052" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c05a08d8162628e21f5cd0f4a253bb7a2733fb49041e999778716cebcb87e247"} {"question" "q-114052" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-114052" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{2}x)+C"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{2}x)+C"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{arcsec}(x)+C"] ["math" "\\text{arcsec}(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{2}})+C"] ["math" "\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{2}x)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-114052" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{2}x)+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-49555" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{1}{6|x|\\sqrt{36{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-49555" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{6|x|\\sqrt{36{x}^{2}-1}}=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{|6x|\\sqrt{(6x)^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nThis integral now resembles the basic one for $\\text{arcsec},$\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $6x.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=6x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{6}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{6|x|\\sqrt{36{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{|6x|\\sqrt{(6x)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{6}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(6x)}{6}+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-49555" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c05a08d8162628e21f5cd0f4a253bb7a2733fb49041e999778716cebcb87e247"} {"question" "q-49555" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-49555" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(6x)}{6}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(36x)}{6}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(6x)}{6}+C"] ["math" "\\text{arcsec}(36x)+C"] ["math" "\\text{arcsec}(6x)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-49555" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(6x)}{6}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-19397" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{7}\\frac{9}{2+8{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-19397" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{7}\\frac{9}{2+8{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{7}\\frac{1}{1+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $4{x}^{2}=(2x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=2x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $14$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{7}\\frac{9}{2+8{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{7}\\frac{1}{1+(2x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{14}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{14}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u{|}_{0}^{14} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(14)-\\frac{9}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(14)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-19397" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c05a08d8162628e21f5cd0f4a253bb7a2733fb49041e999778716cebcb87e247"} {"question" "q-19397" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-19397" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "9\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(14)"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(14)"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(7)"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(14)"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(7)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-19397" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(14)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-19393" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{16-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-19393" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{16-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =5{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{16\\cdot (1-{x}^{2}/16)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/16}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/4)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{4})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{4}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=4\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{16-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{5}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/4)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (4\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =5{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})-5\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-19393" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c05a08d8162628e21f5cd0f4a253bb7a2733fb49041e999778716cebcb87e247"} {"question" "q-19393" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-19393" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{5\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{5\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{5\\pi }{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{6}"] ["math" "\\pi "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-19393" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5\\pi }{6}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-19394" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-19394" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2\\cdot (1-{x}^{2}/2)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/\\sqrt{2})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{2}})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{2}}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/\\sqrt{2})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}/2} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})-2\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-19394" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c05a08d8162628e21f5cd0f4a253bb7a2733fb49041e999778716cebcb87e247"} {"question" "q-19394" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-19394" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-19394" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-351291" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{5-80{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-351291" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{5-80{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =10{\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5(1-16{x}^{2})}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{5}}{\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-16{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(4x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine, \n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(4x)}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=4x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{5-80{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\sqrt{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(4x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u\\,{|}_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{6}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi \\sqrt{5}}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-351291" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c05a08d8162628e21f5cd0f4a253bb7a2733fb49041e999778716cebcb87e247"} {"question" "q-351291" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-351291" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{12}\\sqrt{5}\\pi"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-19396" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1/5}\\frac{20}{3+75{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-19396" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that we can write this integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1/5}\\frac{20}{3+75{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{20}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1/5}\\frac{1}{1+25{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $25{x}^{2}=(5x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=5x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=5\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/5}\\frac{20}{3+75{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{20}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1/5}\\frac{1}{1+(5x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)-\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-19396" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c05a08d8162628e21f5cd0f4a253bb7a2733fb49041e999778716cebcb87e247"} {"question" "q-19396" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-19396" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{4\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "q-19396" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi }{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/state.json" "file_sha256" "00a402c4f99ff24ec0818764e83e44b23d99917aab7104645f3efeb7e84e6a30"} {"question" "e-470" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{9}{4\\sqrt{1-9x^2}} \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/example-470.json" "file_sha256" "1025a33422822b6db8f473989eb2074d5d9763952048ca4f593096ef1da5e7e2"} {"question" "e-470" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^2}}\\textrm{d}u = \\arcsin(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u^2$ as the variable, we have $9x^2 = (3x)^2.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=3x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=3\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\dfrac 1 3 \\,\\textrm d u=\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nWe can now write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{9}{4\\sqrt{1-9{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{9}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(3x)^{2}}}\\,\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{12}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot \\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡3x+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/example-470.json" "file_sha256" "1025a33422822b6db8f473989eb2074d5d9763952048ca4f593096ef1da5e7e2"} {"question" "e-471" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral  $\\displaystyle{\\int \\dfrac{3}{2 + 50x^2} \\, \\textrm{d}x }.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/example-471.json" "file_sha256" "252352644dbe0a25fe397efd63f81934562ae8869aa32c079dd3097021d97db2"} {"question" "e-471" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{3}{2 + 50x^2} \\, \\textrm{d}x = \\int \\dfrac{3}{2(1 + 25x^2)} = \\dfrac 3 2 \\int \\dfrac{1}{1+25x^2}\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+u^2}\\textrm{d}u =\\arctan u +C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u^2$ as the variable, we have $25x^2 = (5x)^2.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=5x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=5\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\dfrac 1 5\\,\\textrm d u = \\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nWe can now write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{2+50{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{1+25{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(5x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}\\cdot \\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡5x+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/example-471.json" "file_sha256" "252352644dbe0a25fe397efd63f81934562ae8869aa32c079dd3097021d97db2"} {"question" "e-5014" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{5\\, \\textrm{d}x}{|5x|\\sqrt{(5x)^2-1}}  = }$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/example-5014.json" "file_sha256" "a21fd1bc799688842e857e008530cd6c2e0f3501ce9a0afcec861d7cb117cc11"} {"question" "e-5014" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This resembles the basic integral for $\\textrm{arcsec},$\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{u^2-1}} \\textrm{d}u = \\textrm{arcsec}(u)+C.\n$$\n\nLet $u = 5x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=5\n\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n5\\,\\textrm{d}x = \\textrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5\\,\\text{d}x}{|5x|\\sqrt{(5x)^{2}-1}} & =\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}(u)+C \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}(5x)+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/example-5014.json" "file_sha256" "a21fd1bc799688842e857e008530cd6c2e0f3501ce9a0afcec861d7cb117cc11"} {"question" "e-472" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle{\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt 2} \\dfrac{1}{2+x^2}\\, \\textrm{d}x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/example-472.json" "file_sha256" "03dabd58e40622eb355f9559dc7c36cdabd9fab6dc543fb17c701a650367b3c6"} {"question" "e-472" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{1}{2+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{1}{2(1+{x}^{2}/2)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{1}{2(1+(x/\\sqrt{2})^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{1}{1+(x/\\sqrt{2})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that this integral now resembles the basic integral for the inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int\\dfrac{1}{1+u^2}\\,\\textrm d u = \\arctan{u} + C.\n$$\n\nWe make the substitution $u=\\dfrac{x}{\\sqrt 2}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\sqrt 2 \\,\\textrm d u = \\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{1}{2+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡1-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi \\sqrt{2}}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005939/example-472.json" "file_sha256" "03dabd58e40622eb355f9559dc7c36cdabd9fab6dc543fb17c701a650367b3c6"}] "usage" {"q-19397" [] "q-19394" [] "e-472" [] "e-5014" [] "e-471" [] "q-2505" [] "e-470" []} "basis" 1110 "retractions" [[17592186064563 :question/problem "What is $∫\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - 4x^{2}}}dx$?"] [17592186064461 :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $∫_{0}^{7}\\frac{9}{2 + 8x^{2}}dx$."] [17592186064460 :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $∫_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2 - x^{2}}}dx$."] [17592186064003 :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{9}{4\\sqrt{1-9x^2}} \\, \\textrm{d}x$."] [17592186064003 :question/worked-solution "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^2}}\\textrm{d}u = \\arcsin(u)+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u^2$ as the variable, we have\n\n$$\n9x^2 = (3x)^2\n$$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=3x$. Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=3\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\dfrac 1 3 \\,\\textrm d u=\\textrm d x\n$$\n\nWe can now write the integral in terms of $u$, and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫\\frac{9}{4\\sqrt{1 - 9x^{2}}}dx &= \\frac{9}{4}∫(1)/(\\sqrt{1 - (3x)^{2}})dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{9}{4}∫\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}} \\cdot \\frac{1}{3}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{9}{12}∫\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{4} \\cdot \\arcsin u + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{4}\\arcsin 3x + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186064004 :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle{\\int \\dfrac{3}{2 + 50x^2} \\, \\textrm{d}x}$."] [17592186064004 :question/worked-solution "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{3}{2 + 50x^2} \\, \\textrm{d}x = \\int \\dfrac{3}{2(1 + 25x^2)} = \\dfrac 3 2 \\int \\dfrac{1}{1+25x^2}\\,\\textrm d x\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+u^2}\\textrm{d}u =\\arctan u +C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u^2$ as the variable, we have\n\n$$\n25x^2 = (5x)^2\n$$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=5x$. Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=5\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\dfrac 1 5\\,\\textrm d u = \\textrm d x\n$$\n\nWe can now write the integral in terms of $u$, and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫\\frac{3}{2 + 50x^{2}}dx &= \\frac{3}{2}∫\\frac{1}{1 + 25x^{2}}dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{2}∫(1)/(1 + (5x)^{2})dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{2}∫\\frac{1}{1 + u^{2}} \\cdot \\frac{1}{5}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{10}∫\\frac{1}{1 + u^{2}}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{10} \\cdot \\arctan u + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{10}\\arctan 5x + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186064014 :question/problem "${\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{5\\, \\textrm{d}x}{\\mid 5x \\mid \\sqrt{(5x)^2-1}} =}$"] [17592186064014 :question/worked-solution "This resembles the basic integral for $\\textrm{arcsec}$,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\mid u \\mid \\sqrt{u^2-1}} \\textrm{d}u = \\textrm{arcsec}(u)+C\n$$\n\nLet $u = 5x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=5 \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad 5\\,\\textrm{d}x = \\textrm{d}u\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫(5dx)/(\\begin{vmatrix}5x & \\sqrt{(5x)^{2} - 1}) &= ∫\\frac{du}{\\mid u\\end{vmatrix}\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1}} \\\\\n&= arcsec(u) + C \\\\\n&= arcsec(5x) + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186064005 :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle{\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt 2} \\dfrac{1}{2+x^2}\\, \\textrm{d}x}$."] [17592186064005 :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{1}{2 + x^{2}}dx &= ∫_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}(1)/(2(1 + x^{2}/2))dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}(1)/(2(1 + (x/\\sqrt{2})^{2}))dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}∫_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}(1)/(1 + (x/\\sqrt{2})^{2})dx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that this integral now resembles the basic integral for the inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int\\dfrac{1}{1+u^2}\\,\\textrm d u = \\arctan{u} + C\n$$\n\nWe make the substitution\n\n$$\nu=\\dfrac{x}{\\sqrt 2}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\sqrt 2 \\,\\textrm d u = \\textrm d x\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u$.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt2$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$, and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{1}{2 + x^{2}}dx &= \\frac{1}{2}∫_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1 + u^{2}} \\cdot \\sqrt{2}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}∫_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1 + u^{2}}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\arctan u \\mid _{0}^{1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(\\arctan 1 - \\arctan 0) \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(\\frac{π}{4} - 0) \\\\\n&= \\frac{π\\sqrt{2}}{8}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186061410 17592186061411 17592186061412 17592186061413 17592186061414 17592186061416 17592186061417 17592186061418 17592186061419 17592186061420 17592186061890 17592186061891 17592186061892 17592186061893 17592186061894] "immutable_fields" [[17592186061409 :answer-field/correct] [17592186061409 :answer-field/id] [17592186061409 :answer-field/key] [17592186061409 :answer-field/type] [17592186061415 :answer-field/correct] [17592186061415 :answer-field/id] [17592186061415 :answer-field/key] [17592186061415 :answer-field/type] [17592186061889 :answer-field/correct] [17592186061889 :answer-field/id] [17592186061889 :answer-field/key] [17592186061889 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
